---
title: Traditional Steam-Baked Challah
servings: 10
prepTime: 3 hr
cookTime: 30 min
source: https://oven.anovaculinary.com/recipe/ZC2mfYx13r4Tg59lkE7j
tags: Bread, Steam Oven, CSO
---

> Note: This recipe was adapted from the Anova steam oven, 
> so the cooking mode settings are not directly comparable.
> Watch the bread near the end of the cooking process to not over-bake.

In a large bowl, whisk together the @water{1%cup}(plus 1 Tbsp, lukewarm 100-110°F)
and @instant yeast{1.75%tsp} until dissolved.

Add @all-purpose flour{1/2%lb}(sifted) to the bowl with the yeast-water mixture.
Add the @granulated sugar{1/3%cup}, @oil{3%Tbsp}(neutral flavor), @egg yolk{1}(extra large), and @salt{1.5%tsp}.
Stir until homogenous and soupy.

Add another @all-purpose flour{1/2%lb}(sifted).
Mix until it gets little tougher than before.
Add the remaining @all-purpose flour{1/2%lb}(sifted) and mix until you cannot mix any longer.

Transfer the dough to a lightly floured counter and knead by hand until smooth and elastic, at least ~{12%minutes}.

Transfer to a clean large bowl. Cover and let rise in a warm place until doubled in size, ~{2-3%hours}.

The bread can be made with a 4-braid or 6-braid pattern.
Divide the dough into 4 or 6 pieces, respectively, and roll each into 12-inch-long strands.
Braid, following the directions in the video, placing the loaf on the solid convection oven pan.
Let rest for ~{30%minutes} before baking.

Insert the modular rack near the middle of the #convection steam oven{}.
While the braided loaf rests, preheat the oven on Convection Steam mode at 350°F.

Transfer to the oven and bake until fully cooked and the top is crisp, about ~{30%minutes}.

Let cool completely before serving.
